          "text": "The pattern indexes best as a **triclinic, centrosymmetric FePSe phase**, space group \\(P\\overline{1}\\) (No. 2), with \\(Z=2\\). The cell is pseudo-monoclinic and consistent with an ordered arsenopyrite/ullmannite-related P\u2013Se dimer structure.\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 16.74\u00b0 | 100 |\n| 22.74\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 22.89\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 24.19\u00b0 | 011 |\n| 31.05\u00b0 | 1\u221210 |\n| 31.29\u00b0 | 10\u22121 |\n| 33.85\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 36.56\u00b0 | \u2212111 |\n| 40.72\u00b0 | 021 |\n| 43.31\u00b0 | 020 |\n\nThe lattice is considerably better constrained than the internal coordinates; the latter should be regarded as a chemically constrained powder solution pending Rietveld refinement.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_FePSe_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing and chemically constrained direct-space solution'\n_audit_creation_date              2025-01-01\n\n_chemical_name_common             'iron phosphorus selenide'\n_chemical_formula_sum             'Fe P Se'\n_chemical_formula_structural      'FePSe'\n_cell_formula_units_Z             2\n_formula_weight                   165.790\n\n_space_group_crystal_system       triclinic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'P -1'\n_space_group_IT_number            2\n\n_cell_length_a                    6.295\n_cell_length_b                    5.074\n_cell_length_c                    5.018\n_cell_angle_alpha                 59.80\n_cell_angle_beta                  61.96\n_cell_angle_gamma                 62.02\n_cell_volume                      116.4\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn     4.73\n_diffrn_radiation_type            'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength      1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,-y,-z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nFe1 Fe 1 a  0.0000  0.0000  0.0000  1.0  0.50\nFe2 Fe 1 h  0.5000  0.5000  0.5000  1.0  0.50\nP1  P  2 i  0.1848  0.1452  0.1804  1.0  0.60\nSe1 Se 2 i  0.3449  0.3051  0.3402  1.0  0.55\n```\n\nA metrically related pseudo-monoclinic \\(C\\)-centered supercell can be constructed with approximately \\(a=6.30\\), \\(b=5.03\\), \\(c=8.75\\) \u00c5 and \\(\\beta\\approx122.8^\\circ\\), but the resolved peak splitting favors the triclinic model rather than an exact monoclinic alternative.",
